---

Third-party code and attribution:

* The SF900 / SF2000 2.4 GHz RF protocol (addresses, hop channels, register
  configuration, button map) was reverse-engineered by the axgdev/UniFrog
  project (MIT License) — https://github.com/axgdev/UniFrog . This project
  reimplements that protocol for the ESP32 + XN297L. Huge thanks to axgdev.

* firmware/esp32s3-wifi-dongle is based on Espressif's esp-iot-solution
  "usb_dongle" example (Apache-2.0) — https://github.com/espressif/esp-iot-solution .
  The bundled components/ (tinyusb_dongle, FreeRTOS-Plus-CLI) retain their
  original licenses; see the LICENSE files within those directories.

* XN297L register/calibration values cross-referenced against the Panchip
  XN297L datasheet and public native drivers.
